 "title": "A growing law needs a shared coin: refinement shares it, accretion must carry it",
 "subject": "Whether a law that grows the two-kind knot spheres can make them round without a hidden witness",
 "conclusion": "Growth keeps a knot sphere round without a witness only by refinement, which scales an already round seed and never places a corner. Accretion must place corners, and when each turn is decided by a label-free local rule it also closes lopsided spheres, so making the four equator corners agree needs a bit carried by the process, a hidden witness under the canonical test.",
